A structural or ddg_mixed row stands for a group, and its scalar fields
are the first member's. Two consumers read those scalars where the
question is about the group:

- The INV-dudal evaluation-site withdrawal built `reached` from the
  witness sink only, so a group whose witness was a project sink but
  which also reached document.write kept the qualification it must
  withdraw (confirmed_with_caveats where inconclusive is required).
  It now reads every member of sink_primitives, mapped to the
  opaque-site spelling (_qualify's "eval.eval" vs the joined "eval").
- The choice_shaped_source caveat tested the witness source_primitive.
  It now tests source_primitives.

The caveat also said "N of this claim's evidence rows" while counting
distinct names; it now counts rows. It is restricted to untrusted_input,
the label the choice shape was defined on, and erlang's gethostname /
getservbyname / getservbyport (host_info_read since WI-dozul) leave
CHOICE_SHAPED_SOURCE_NAMES.

The three strict xfails WI-ziruv shipped for these (#1902, #1905) now
pass and lose their marks. Each fix was mutated back and its tests
went red.

Addresses WI-kufos, WI-zakil.

